# Onboarding & Authentication Flows

## Overview

DECM supports two registration methods:

1. **Wallet-based** - Web3 wallet signature authentication (MetaMask, WalletConnect, etc.)
2. **OAuth Google** - Traditional OAuth 2.0 with Google

Both flows create an `AuthenticationCredential` → `Profile` → `JWT Session`.

## Architecture

### Frontend Services

- **AuthService** - [apps/web/src/services/AuthService.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/services/AuthService.ts)
  - `createAccount()` - Register new user
  - `createProfile()` - Create user profile
  - `updateProfile()` - Update user profile
  - `signOut()` - Logout user

- **OnboardService** - [apps/web/src/services/OnboardService.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/services/OnboardService.ts)
  - `checkOnboardStatus()` - Check registration progress
  - `getSignMessage()` - Get wallet signature message

### Backend Layers

```
Handler → Usecase → DataGateway (Repository) → Database
```

- **Handler** - [apps/backend/core-api/internal/handler/onboard/](mdc:apps/backend/core-api/internal/handler/onboard/)
  - HTTP request parsing and validation
  - OpenAPI/Swagger documentation
  - Response formatting

- **Usecase** - [apps/backend/core-api/internal/usecase/onboard/onboard.go](mdc:apps/backend/core-api/internal/usecase/onboard/onboard.go)
  - Business logic and validation
  - Signature verification (wallet)
  - OAuth token verification (Google)
  - JWT token generation

- **DataGateway** - Database operations with PII encryption

