## Session Management

### JWT Token Structure

```json
{
    "user_id": "uuid",
    "wallet_address": "0x..." // OR
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "exp": 1234567890,
    "iat": 1234567890
}
```

### Cookie Settings

```go
cookie := &fiber.Cookie{
    Name:     "session",
    Value:    jwt,
    Expires:  time.Now().Add(24 * time.Hour),
    HTTPOnly: true,
    Secure:   true, // HTTPS only in production
    SameSite: "Lax",
}
```

### Local Storage (Frontend)

Stored in [localStorage](mdc:apps/web/src/lib/constants/localStorage.ts):

- `auth-sign-signature` - Wallet signature (wallet flow)
- `access-token` - Google access token (OAuth flow)
- `expires-in` - Token expiration time (OAuth flow)

**Why both cookie AND localStorage?**

- **Cookie**: Sent automatically with API requests (HttpOnly, secure)
- **localStorage**: Client-side state management, onboarding progress

